# The weights of this module go through Git LFS: git keeps a pointer of a few
# lines and the file itself lies beside it in the LFS store. Without this the
# history swells without bound - git holds a whole copy of a two-gigabyte binary
# on every change and shows no diff for it - and a shallow clone of the branch
# stops being possible at all.
#
# WHAT BELONGS HERE is what a recipe cannot express and what changes rarely. A
# converted and quantised model is exactly that: it is the OUTPUT of a conversion
# nobody will run again the same way, so the recipe is not a substitute for the
# file. The cost, stated because it decides the list: LFS does not compress one
# version against another, so every re-conversion is stored whole.
#
# THE LIST IS BY KIND AND NOT BY SIZE. A sentencepiece model is under a megabyte
# today; it is still a binary blob whose diff means nothing, and a rule applied
# only once it hurts is a rule nobody applies.
#
# The repository's own .gitattributes already covers *.dll, *.7z and the plugin
# formats. These are the ones a model mod adds.

# ggml / whisper.cpp and llama.cpp family
*.bin           filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.gguf          filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ggml          filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# the formats a conversion may be taken FROM, so that a checked-in source is not
# the thing that swells the history either
*.safetensors   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pt            filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pth           filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ckpt          filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.npz           filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.onnx          filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# tokenisers and vocabularies that are binary
*.model         filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.spm           filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# SHA256SUMS is TEXT and must never be an LFS pointer. It is the one file that
# has to be readable in a plain clone - it is what says whether the pointers,
# once fetched, brought back the right bytes - and a checksum file behind a
# pointer is a checksum nobody can check.
SHA256SUMS      text eol=lf -filter -diff -merge
